Each star was perfect and still, shining with constant brilliance. But the Sky Goddess noticed something troubling—the stars never spoke, never moved, never showed emotion. They were beautiful but lifeless.

Saddened, she visited the Earth Keeper and asked for advice. The old spirit smiled and gave her a gift: a handful of wind sprites, mischievous creatures who loved to dance and play.

